# AWS Cloud Ops Basics

This repository demonstrates **foundational AWS Cloud Operations tasks** commonly performed by Cloud Ops / Junior Cloud Engineers.  
The focus is on **compute, storage, IAM, monitoring, and cost awareness**, aligned with real-world production support scenarios.

---

## 🔧 Services Covered

- **Amazon EC2** – Instance provisioning & management
- **Amazon S3** – Storage & lifecycle management
- **IAM** – Users, roles, and policies
- **CloudWatch** – Monitoring & alerts
- **AWS CLI** – Basic operational commands
- **Terraform (Basics)** – Infrastructure as Code

---

## 📌 Project Use Cases

### 1️⃣ EC2 Operations
- Launching EC2 instances
- Understanding instance types & cost impact
- Security group basics
- Start/Stop instances for cost optimization

### 2️⃣ IAM Basics
- Creating IAM users & roles
- Attaching least-privilege policies
- Understanding IAM best practices

### 3️⃣ S3 Operations
- Creating S3 buckets
- Uploading & managing objects
- Implementing lifecycle policies
- Cost-effective storage practices

### 4️⃣ CloudWatch Monitoring
- Creating CloudWatch alarms
- Monitoring CPU utilization
- Understanding logs & metrics
- Alerting for operational issues

### 5️⃣ Cost Optimization (Ops Perspective)
- Instance rightsizing awareness
- Storage lifecycle rules
- Monitoring unused resources

